# inc-9smo. Throw one set of bolas at a frozen bugbear three squares away, then
# read the bugbear's own status list (wizard "Examine Nearby Things") before and
# after a long wait. Driven by tools/check_bolas_entangle_expiry.sh, which runs
# it once per seed because the entangle needs a hit AND a failed Reflex save.
#
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/kobold-rogue-seed1.sav \
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/bolas-entangle-expiry.keys <seed>
#
# THE SUBJECT is the frozen kobold rogue: a kobold throws bolas proficiently and
# already carries a set (equipped, so "f a" throws it). Wizard switches: Freeze
# Monsters (row 10) keeps the bugbear from acting, so it makes no escape check
# and no attack of opportunity; Show All Combat Rolls (row 11) puts the rolls in
# the message log. The menu keeps its cursor between openings, so one opening
# does both. A kobold stands three squares away (bolas range 3) after two moves.
#
# THE WAIT is 150 "wait one turn" keys, far past any 2d4-round duration.

w
@expect "Enter wizard mode"
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
DOWN
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "bugbear"
RIGHT
ENTER
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f
LEFT
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" f

f
a
RIGHT
@dump:thrown

# The bugbear's status list, before the wait.
w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@until "bugbear (class" RIGHT
PGDN*40
@dump:before
ESC

.*150

w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@until "bugbear (class" RIGHT
PGDN*40
@dump:after
ESC
v
@dump:log
ESC
@quit
